<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<html>
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8"/>
  </head>
  <body>
    <ul id="vimtest-root">
      <li id="vimtest-001" data-type="heading">
        <p>Vim Keybindings — manual test</p>
        <ul>
          <li id="vimtest-002" data-type="note">
            <p>Generated by scripts/generate-manual-test.ts from the keymap; do not edit by hand. Open Bike &gt; Logs Explorer (check &quot;vim-keybindings&quot;) before starting and watch for [Vim] errors.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-003" data-type="note">
            <p>Press Escape so the selection is a block (row) selection: that is vim normal mode. Multi-key sequences are typed one key after another (yy = y, then y). Tick each task when the described result happened.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-004" data-type="note">
            <p>Tip: u undoes any edit made by a check, so the playground can be restored at any point.</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li id="vimtest-005" data-type="heading">
        <p>Playground — rows the checks below refer to</p>
        <ul>
          <li id="vimtest-006">
            <p>Alpha (has children; collapse it with zc when a check asks for a collapsed row)</p>
            <ul>
              <li id="vimtest-007">
                <p>Alpha 1 (collapse me with zc before the motion checks)</p>
                <ul>
                  <li id="vimtest-008">
                    <p>Alpha 1a (level 3)</p>
                    <ul>
                      <li id="vimtest-009">
                        <p>Alpha 1a-i (level 4, the deepest row)</p>
                      </li>
                    </ul>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </li>
              <li id="vimtest-010" data-type="task" data-done="2026-08-26">
                <p>Alpha 2 (a done task: register round-trips must keep the checkmark)</p>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-011" data-type="heading">
            <p>Beta (a heading row)</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-012">
            <p></p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-013" data-type="quote">
            <p>Delta (a quote row, with <strong>bold</strong> and <code>code</code> runs)</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-014">
            <p>Gamma — the last row of the playground</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li id="vimtest-015" data-type="heading">
        <p>Motions</p>
        <ul>
          <li id="vimtest-016" data-type="task">
            <p><code>j</code> — Select &quot;Alpha&quot; (Playground) and press j: &quot;Alpha 1&quot; is selected. Press j again on a collapsed &quot;Alpha 1&quot;: &quot;Alpha 2&quot; is selected, the hidden &quot;Alpha 1a&quot; is skipped.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-017" data-type="task">
            <p><code>k</code> — From &quot;Beta&quot; press k: &quot;Alpha 2&quot; is selected. On the first row of the document k does nothing.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-018" data-type="task">
            <p><code>h</code> — On an expanded &quot;Alpha&quot; press h: it collapses and stays selected. Press h again: nothing (top level). On &quot;Alpha 2&quot; press h: &quot;Alpha&quot; is selected.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-019" data-type="task">
            <p><code>l</code> — On a collapsed &quot;Alpha&quot; press l: it expands and stays selected. Press l again: &quot;Alpha 1&quot; is selected. On the empty row press l: nothing.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-020" data-type="task">
            <p><code>gg</code> (Bike: <code>g g</code>) — From anywhere press g g: the first row of the document is selected. Press 3 g g: the third visible row.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-021" data-type="task">
            <p><code>G</code> (Bike: <code>shift-g</code>) — From anywhere press G: the last row of the document is selected. Press 2 G: the second visible row.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-022" data-type="task">
            <p><code>J</code> (Bike: <code>shift-j</code>) — On &quot;Beta&quot; press J: &quot;Beta&quot; and the next row are selected. Press K: back to &quot;Beta&quot; only.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-023" data-type="task">
            <p><code>K</code> (Bike: <code>shift-k</code>) — On &quot;Gamma&quot; press K twice: three rows selected upward. Press J: back to two.</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li id="vimtest-024" data-type="heading">
        <p>Counts</p>
        <ul>
          <li id="vimtest-025" data-type="task">
            <p><code>0</code> — Press 0 alone: nothing happens (Bike keeps its own behaviour). Press 1 0 j from the top: ten rows down, or the last row.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-026" data-type="task">
            <p><code>1</code> (Bike: <code>1-9</code>) — Press 3 then j from &quot;Alpha&quot;: &quot;Beta&quot; is selected (three visible rows down).</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li id="vimtest-027" data-type="heading">
        <p>Folding and hoisting</p>
        <ul>
          <li id="vimtest-028" data-type="task">
            <p><code>zo</code> (Bike: <code>z o</code>) — On a collapsed &quot;Alpha&quot; press z o: it expands.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-029" data-type="task">
            <p><code>zc</code> (Bike: <code>z c</code>) — On an expanded &quot;Alpha&quot; press z c: it collapses; &quot;Alpha 1&quot; and &quot;Alpha 2&quot; disappear.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-030" data-type="task">
            <p><code>za</code> (Bike: <code>z a</code>) — Press z a twice on &quot;Alpha&quot;: collapsed, then expanded again.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-031" data-type="task">
            <p><code>zR</code> (Bike: <code>z shift-r</code>) — Collapse a few rows, press z R: everything expands.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-032" data-type="task">
            <p><code>zM</code> (Bike: <code>z shift-m</code>) — Press z M: every row with children collapses. Press z R to recover.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-033" data-type="task">
            <p><code>L</code> (Bike: <code>shift-l</code>) — On &quot;Alpha&quot; press L: the editor focuses in on Alpha (its children become the top level). Press H: focus out to the whole document.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-034" data-type="task">
            <p><code>H</code> (Bike: <code>shift-h</code>) — While focused in, press H: back out one level. At the document level H does nothing.</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li id="vimtest-035" data-type="heading">
        <p>Operators</p>
        <ul>
          <li id="vimtest-036" data-type="task">
            <p><code>yy</code> (Bike: <code>y y</code>) — On &quot;Alpha&quot; press y y: nothing visible changes, selection stays. Then on &quot;Gamma&quot; press p: a copy of Alpha with all its children, still a heading, appears after Gamma.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-037" data-type="task">
            <p><code>yj</code> (Bike: <code>y j</code>) — On &quot;Alpha 2&quot; press y j: selection stays on Alpha 2. On &quot;Gamma&quot; press p: &quot;Alpha 2&quot; and &quot;Beta&quot; appear after Gamma.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-038" data-type="task">
            <p><code>yk</code> (Bike: <code>y k</code>) — On &quot;Beta&quot; press y k: then p pastes &quot;Alpha 2&quot; (hmm: Alpha 2 is a child) and &quot;Beta&quot; as siblings after the current row.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-039" data-type="task">
            <p><code>ygg</code> (Bike: <code>y g g</code>) — On &quot;Beta&quot; press y g g, then G and p: everything from the document start through Beta is pasted at the end (rows inside a copied parent are not duplicated).</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-040" data-type="task">
            <p><code>yG</code> (Bike: <code>y shift-g</code>) — On &quot;Beta&quot; press y G, then g g and P: Beta through the last row are pasted at the top.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-041" data-type="task">
            <p><code>dd</code> (Bike: <code>d d</code>) — On &quot;Alpha 2&quot; (a @done task) press d d: it disappears, &quot;Beta&quot; is selected. Press P: it comes back above Beta, still done. Press u: paste undone.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-042" data-type="task">
            <p><code>dj</code> (Bike: <code>d j</code>) — On &quot;Beta&quot; press d j: Beta and the row below vanish. On the last row of the document d j does nothing.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-043" data-type="task">
            <p><code>dk</code> (Bike: <code>d k</code>) — On &quot;Gamma&quot; press d k: Gamma and the row above vanish; the row before them is selected.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-044" data-type="task">
            <p><code>dgg</code> (Bike: <code>d g g</code>) — On the second row press d g g: the first two rows vanish. Press u to undo.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-045" data-type="task">
            <p><code>dG</code> (Bike: <code>d shift-g</code>) — On &quot;Gamma&quot; press d G: everything from Gamma to the end vanishes; the previous row is selected. Press u to undo.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-046" data-type="task">
            <p><code>cc</code> (Bike: <code>c c</code>) — On &quot;Beta&quot; press c c: the text clears, the row keeps its heading style, the caret blinks at the start and the status bar shows -- INSERT --. Type something, press Escape. Press p: the old &quot;Beta&quot; is pasted below.</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li id="vimtest-047" data-type="heading">
        <p>Register (yank / paste)</p>
        <ul>
          <li id="vimtest-048" data-type="task">
            <p><code>p</code> — After y y on &quot;Alpha&quot;, press p on &quot;Alpha 1&quot;: the copy is inserted after &quot;Alpha 2&quot; (after the whole Alpha subtree is NOT expected; p pastes after the selected row's own subtree, so after Alpha 1). Press 3 p: three copies.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-049" data-type="task">
            <p><code>P</code> (Bike: <code>shift-p</code>) — Press P on &quot;Gamma&quot;: the register is pasted above Gamma and the pasted row is selected.</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li id="vimtest-050" data-type="heading">
        <p>Insert mode</p>
        <ul>
          <li id="vimtest-051" data-type="task">
            <p><code>i</code> — On &quot;Beta&quot; press i: caret at the start of Beta, status bar -- INSERT --. Type, then Escape: Beta is selected as a block again and the message disappears.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-052" data-type="task">
            <p><code>I</code> (Bike: <code>shift-i</code>) — Same as i.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-053" data-type="task">
            <p><code>a</code> — On &quot;Beta&quot; press a: caret at the end of Beta.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-054" data-type="task">
            <p><code>A</code> (Bike: <code>shift-a</code>) — Same as a.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-055" data-type="task">
            <p><code>o</code> — On an expanded &quot;Alpha&quot; press o: a new empty first child appears with the caret in it. On &quot;Gamma&quot; press o: a new sibling below. Escape.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-056" data-type="task">
            <p><code>O</code> (Bike: <code>shift-o</code>) — On &quot;Beta&quot; press O: a new empty row appears above Beta with the caret in it. Escape.</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li id="vimtest-057" data-type="heading">
        <p>Mode transitions</p>
        <ul>
          <li id="vimtest-058" data-type="task">
            <p><code>v</code> — On &quot;Beta&quot; press v: the status bar shows -- VISUAL --. Press j: two rows selected. Press v: back to one row, message gone.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-059" data-type="task">
            <p><code>V</code> (Bike: <code>shift-v</code>) — Same as v.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-060" data-type="task">
            <p><code>Esc</code> (Bike: <code>escape</code>) — With two rows selected via J, press Escape: only the head row stays selected and Bike does NOT switch to text mode. Press Escape again: still block mode.</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li id="vimtest-061" data-type="heading">
        <p>Bike commands on vim keys</p>
        <ul>
          <li id="vimtest-062" data-type="task">
            <p><code>u</code> — After any edit press u: it is undone.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-063" data-type="task">
            <p><code>Ctrl-r</code> (Bike: <code>control-r</code>) — After u press Control-r: redone.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-064" data-type="task">
            <p><code>/</code> — Press /: Bike find opens. Type &quot;Beta&quot;, Return. Escape back to the editor.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-065" data-type="task">
            <p><code>n</code> — After a search press n: next match. Press N: previous match.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-066" data-type="task">
            <p><code>N</code> (Bike: <code>shift-n</code>) — See n.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-067" data-type="task">
            <p><code>&gt;&gt;</code> (Bike: <code>shift-&gt; shift-&gt;</code>) — On &quot;Beta&quot; press &gt; &gt;: Beta indents under the row above. Press &lt; &lt;: back out.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-068" data-type="task">
            <p><code>&lt;&lt;</code> (Bike: <code>shift-&lt; shift-&lt;</code>) — See &gt;&gt;.</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li id="vimtest-069" data-type="heading">
        <p>Visual mode</p>
        <ul>
          <li id="vimtest-070" data-type="task">
            <p><code>j</code> — Select &quot;Alpha&quot; (Playground) and press j: &quot;Alpha 1&quot; is selected. Press j again on a collapsed &quot;Alpha 1&quot;: &quot;Alpha 2&quot; is selected, the hidden &quot;Alpha 1a&quot; is skipped.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-071" data-type="task">
            <p><code>k</code> — From &quot;Beta&quot; press k: &quot;Alpha 2&quot; is selected. On the first row of the document k does nothing.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-072" data-type="task">
            <p><code>gg</code> (Bike: <code>g g</code>) — From anywhere press g g: the first row of the document is selected. Press 3 g g: the third visible row.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-073" data-type="task">
            <p><code>G</code> (Bike: <code>shift-g</code>) — From anywhere press G: the last row of the document is selected. Press 2 G: the second visible row.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-074" data-type="task">
            <p><code>J</code> (Bike: <code>shift-j</code>) — On &quot;Beta&quot; press J: &quot;Beta&quot; and the next row are selected. Press K: back to &quot;Beta&quot; only.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-075" data-type="task">
            <p><code>K</code> (Bike: <code>shift-k</code>) — On &quot;Gamma&quot; press K twice: three rows selected upward. Press J: back to two.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-076" data-type="task">
            <p><code>y</code> — v, j, then y: two rows yanked, visual mode ends, the first of the two is selected. p on &quot;Gamma&quot; pastes both.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-077" data-type="task">
            <p><code>d</code> — v, j, then d: both rows vanish, visual mode ends. P brings them back.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-078" data-type="task">
            <p><code>x</code> — Same as d.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-079" data-type="task">
            <p><code>c</code> — v, j, then c: both rows are replaced by one empty row in insert mode. Escape, then u u to recover.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-080" data-type="task">
            <p><code>p</code> — y y on &quot;Alpha&quot;, then v and j on &quot;Beta&quot;, then p: Beta and the next row are replaced by a copy of Alpha; a following p pastes the replaced rows back.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-081" data-type="task">
            <p><code>P</code> (Bike: <code>shift-p</code>) — Press P on &quot;Gamma&quot;: the register is pasted above Gamma and the pasted row is selected.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-082" data-type="task">
            <p><code>&gt;</code> (Bike: <code>shift-&gt;</code>) — Indent the selected rows</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-083" data-type="task">
            <p><code>&lt;</code> (Bike: <code>shift-&lt;</code>) — Outdent the selected rows</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-084" data-type="task">
            <p><code>i</code> — On &quot;Beta&quot; press i: caret at the start of Beta, status bar -- INSERT --. Type, then Escape: Beta is selected as a block again and the message disappears.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-085" data-type="task">
            <p><code>a</code> — On &quot;Beta&quot; press a: caret at the end of Beta.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-086" data-type="task">
            <p><code>v</code> — On &quot;Beta&quot; press v: the status bar shows -- VISUAL --. Press j: two rows selected. Press v: back to one row, message gone.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-087" data-type="task">
            <p><code>V</code> (Bike: <code>shift-v</code>) — Same as v.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-088" data-type="task">
            <p><code>Esc</code> (Bike: <code>escape</code>) — With two rows selected via J, press Escape: only the head row stays selected and Bike does NOT switch to text mode. Press Escape again: still block mode.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-089" data-type="task">
            <p><code>u</code> — After any edit press u: it is undone.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-090" data-type="task">
            <p><code>Ctrl-r</code> (Bike: <code>control-r</code>) — After u press Control-r: redone.</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li id="vimtest-091" data-type="heading">
        <p>Palette-only commands</p>
        <ul>
          <li id="vimtest-092" data-type="task">
            <p><code>vim:toggle-keybindings</code> — Turn the vim keybindings off or on without disabling the extension</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-093" data-type="task">
            <p><code>vim:toggle-mode-indicator</code> — Show or hide the -- INSERT -- / -- VISUAL -- status bar message</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li id="vimtest-094" data-type="heading">
        <p>Extension lifecycle</p>
        <ul>
          <li id="vimtest-095" data-type="task">
            <p>Escape from insert mode using Bike's own handling (no vim binding in text mode): the -- INSERT -- message disappears and vim keys work again immediately.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-096" data-type="task">
            <p>Bike &gt; Extensions Explorer: disable Vim Keybindings. j/k/dd do what Bike does by default (nothing vim-ish). Re-enable: vim keys are back without restarting Bike.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-097" data-type="task">
            <p>Command palette (⇧⌘P) › &quot;Vim: Toggle Keybindings&quot;: same as above but without disabling the extension; the status bar confirms on/off. Toggle back on.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-098" data-type="task">
            <p>Command palette › &quot;Vim: Toggle Mode Indicator&quot;: the -- INSERT -- / -- VISUAL -- messages stop; toggle again to restore.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-099" data-type="task">
            <p>Two windows: y y a row in this document, open another document, p there: the row (with children) is pasted. The register is shared.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-100" data-type="task">
            <p>Visual mode then switch window: v here, click another window, come back: visual mode is off (no -- VISUAL --, y needs y y again).</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-101" data-type="task">
            <p>Click into a row while in visual mode: the caret appears, -- VISUAL -- goes away, -- INSERT -- shows.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-102" data-type="task">
            <p>Bike &gt; Logs Explorer with &quot;vim-keybindings&quot; checked: no [Vim] errors appeared during this pass.</p>
          </li>
          <li id="vimtest-103" data-type="task">
            <p>Keys the extension does not bind (for example x in normal mode, or w, b, e) still do whatever Bike does by default.</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </body>
</html>
